# --- Ephemeral probe scratchpad ---
# Every session's one-off probes land here. It was ALREADY treated as gitignored by NOTES, by
# ARCHITECTURE, and by tests/test_citations.py — and it was NOT, merely untracked. The effect was
# the same (probes never survive a session) but the CLAIM was false, which is the exact disease
# test_citations.py exists to kill. Making it true rather than rewording the claim: a probe that
# matters enough to cite belongs in scripts/, committed. See NOTES "FABRICATED VERIFICATION
# CITATIONS" and test_citations.py rule (C).
scratchpad/
**/scratchpad/

# --- Lambda build artifacts (rebuilt from build.py; wheels are large) ---
lambda/*/package/
lambda/*/*.zip


audit.md
FRONTEND.md

# --- Corpus data ---
# data/raw/ holds the source PDFs and the 475MB IBM CSV — never committed.
# data/corpus/ holds the PARSED MARKDOWN, and it IS committed, deliberately. It is a derived
# artifact, but it is the INGEST'S ACTUAL INPUT: scripts/ingest_regulatory.py reads these files,
# not the PDFs. Committing them is what makes the regulatory ingest reproducible by someone with
# no LlamaParse key, and it keeps llama-cloud-services (67 packages; it upgrades SQLAlchemy and
# numpy out from under the app) out of requirements.txt entirely. Re-derive with
# scripts/parse_regulatory.py in an ISOLATED venv. See NOTES "The regulatory corpus".
#
# NOTE THE SHAPE: `data/*`, not `data/`. Git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a
# later `!data/corpus/` cannot re-include anything under it — the negation is silently dead and
# the markdown stays ignored while .gitignore reads as though it does not. Verified by running
# `git check-ignore`, which is the only thing that settles this. (See NOTES: the same class of
# defect as scratchpad/ being asserted-ignored but merely untracked, in the opposite direction.)
data/*
!data/corpus/
!data/corpus/*.md

# Frontend measurement scratch — NEVER committed, and now it cannot be committed by accident.
#
# `shots/` is screenshot + DOM-snapshot output from driving the console for a Raven audit
# (regenerable, binary, per-session). `drive.mjs` is the Playwright harness that produces it.
#
# THESE WERE UNTRACKED ONLY BECAUSE I REMEMBERED TO DELETE THEM, and that is exactly the failure
# `scripts/serve.py` recorded: a workaround that must be re-derived on every rebuild is not a fix.
# The driver was re-derived TWICE in the Rung 2 session alone. If a later session wants it
# permanently, promote it to `frontend/scripts/` AND declare `playwright` as a devDependency —
# it is currently present only transitively, so a fresh `npm ci` would not have it. That is a
# dependency change and a plan-gated decision, not a drive-by.
frontend/shots/
frontend/drive.mjs
frontend/dbg.mjs
